1) Instalar PHP manager for IIS de web platform installer (install php 5.3.5
   Habilitar CGI
    Control Panel > Programs Ad features > turn windows features on or off
    Server Manager > Roles > Add Role services (select role services) select CGI
    if there are problems with the configuration file see http://support.microsoft.com/kb/942055

    possible premission problems. The file that contains the website's code needs to have appropiate permissions.
    properties > security > Group or user names: SYSTEM, win\alce, win\Administradores win\Usuarios win\IIS_IUSRS

    php.ini:
      enable short_open_tag
      error reporting

    possible erros:
      Deprecated: Call-time pass-by-reference has been deprecated
      set allow_call_time_pass_reference to true in your INI file

      Deprecated: Assigning the return value of new by reference is deprecated
      error_reporting(0)

    server variables may not be the same.
      $_SERVER['xxxx']


   no platform installation:
   http://learn.iis.net/page.aspx/246/using-fastcgi-to-host-php-applications-on-iis-7/

2) Install php drivers for php
   Install sqls server 2008 r2 feature pack
   http://www.microsoft.com/downloads/en/details.aspx?FamilyID=80e44913-24b4-4113-8807-caae6cf2ca05




1) Run php_info in IIS ok
2) Run the app in IIS & mysql ok
3) Run the app in osx. clean up and orginize code and assets
4) Run the app again in IIS & mysql

5) Configure IIS, mysql & MSSQL (run simple app)
6) See if phpmy admin can dump a file that can be read by MSSQL
7) Learn MSSQL equivalent to mysql's source or <
8) Create mssql equivalent to mysqldump
9) Investigate about views
10) Start migration


Local SQLServer instalation
  -named instance SQLExpress
  -instance ID SQLExpress
  -SERvice accounts: SQL Server Database Engine NT AUTHORITY\NETWORK SERVICE
  -Authentication mode Mixed mode
  -sa (server system administrator) password 52546064
  -user alce is server administrator

